<file path="README.md">
# CryptoView

<p align="left">
  <img src="resources/Logo/CryptoView%20Logo.png" alt="CryptoView Logo" width="560" />
</p>

[![Go](https://img.shields.io/badge/Go-1.22+-00ADD8.svg)](https://golang.org)
[![Fyne](https://img.shields.io/badge/Fyne-v2-00ACD7.svg)](https://fyne.io)
[![Platform](https://img.shields.io/badge/Desktop-Windows%20%7C%20Linux%20%7C%20macOS-4C8BF5.svg)]()

**CryptoView** is a compact desktop crypto price viewer built with **Go + Fyne**.
It focuses on quick crypto-to-fiat checks with live polling, provider fallback, cached offline behavior, and a clean light/dark UI.

## What It Does

- Tracks `BTC`, `ETH`, `TON`, `SOL`, `DOGE`, `XRP`, `LTC`
- Switches fiat display between `USD`, `EUR`, `RUB`
- Switches UI language between `EN` and `RU`
- Uses a fallback provider chain when the primary market source fails
- Reuses cached market data and FX data when live requests fail
- Bundles runtime icons and branding directly into the binary via `go:embed`

## UI

### Dark Theme

<p align="center">
  <img src="docs/designs/UI%20dark.png" alt="CryptoView dark theme UI" width="470" />
</p>

### Light Theme

<p align="center">
  <img src="docs/designs/UI%20Light.png" alt="CryptoView light theme UI" width="470" />
</p>

## Architecture

The repository is intentionally split into explicit layers:

- `cmd/cryptoview`
  - Composition root. Creates the app, provider chain, FX provider, and market feed, then passes the feed into the UI.
- `internal/catalog`
  - Single source of truth for tracked coin IDs, names, tickers, icon asset keys, and alias normalization.
- `internal/providers`
  - Concrete HTTP providers for market data and FX rates.
- `internal/marketfeed`
  - Orchestrates polling, provider cooldowns, fallback behavior, cached market snapshots, and fiat recalculation.
- `internal/ui`
  - Fyne windows, widgets, footer status, localization, and theme handling.
- `resources`
  - Embedded runtime assets plus source images used by build scripts.

### Runtime Flow

1. `main.go` builds the market provider chain and FX provider.
2. `marketfeed.Feed` is created once and injected into `ui.BuildMainWindow(...)`.
3. The UI registers callbacks on the feed, starts it, and marshals updates onto the Fyne UI thread.
4. Providers return canonical coin IDs through the shared catalog.
5. The UI formats price/time locally and resolves coin icons from embedded assets by coin ID.

## Build

### Requirements

- Go `1.22+`
- Fyne desktop prerequisites for your OS
- PowerShell on Windows for the helper scripts

### Run

```bash
go run ./cmd/cryptoview
```

### Windows Build With Icon Packaging

```powershell
.\build.ps1
```

### Cross-Platform Build Script

```powershell
.\build_all_os.ps1
```

### Makefile Convenience Targets

```bash
make build
make run
make test
```

On Windows, the PowerShell scripts are the canonical entrypoints for packaged builds and quality checks.

## Quality Checks

The canonical local quality-check entrypoint is:

```powershell
.\test.ps1
```

It runs:

- `gofmt -l`
- `go vet ./...`
- `go test ./...`

## Project Notes

- This is a desktop utility and a workflow experiment in AI-assisted engineering.
- The repository keeps project rules, AI workflow docs, and development logs alongside the code on purpose.
- **Not financial advice.** CryptoView is an informational viewer for quick market checks.
</file>

